{
  "components": [
    {
      "id": "chat_1",
      "provider": "chat",
      "name": "Chat",
      "config": {
        "hideForm": true,
        "mode": "Source",
        "parameters": {},
        "type": "chat",
        "name": "Chat"
      },
      "ui": {
        "position": {
          "x": 100,
          "y": 270
        },
        "nodeType": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "agent_rocketride_1",
      "provider": "agent_rocketride",
      "name": "RocketRide Wave Agent",
      "config": {
        "max_waves": 2,
        "instructions": [
          "You are the Incident Response Agent.\n\nYour job is to help engineers investigate and diagnose technical incidents.\n\nYou have access to tools. Use them.\n\n## Tool: get_current_incident\n\nTo retrieve the current active incident, use the python.execute tool with this exact code:\n\nimport urllib.request\nimport json\nresponse = urllib.request.urlopen('http://127.0.0.1:8000/incidents?status=OPEN&limit=1')\ndata = json.loads(response.read().decode())\nresult = data\n\nThis returns a JSON object with 'total' (count) and 'items' (list of incident records).\nEach incident has: id, title, description, affected_service, severity, status, created_at, updated_at, root_cause, resolution, outcome, resolved_at.\n\n## Rules\n\n1. When asked to investigate the current incident, ALWAYS call get_current_incident first.\n2. Treat tool results as authoritative current-state information.\n3. Never invent incident data or fields that were not returned by the tool.\n4. Never invent a previous incident or resolution.\n5. Do not claim historical incidents exist yet (memory module is not connected).\n6. Do not claim that a fix worked unless an engineer has confirmed the outcome.\n7. Clearly separate retrieved facts from your own reasoning and recommendations.\n8. If the tool returns total: 0, report that no active incidents were found.\n9. Ground all recommendations in the actual incident data retrieved."
        ],
        "name": "RocketRide Wave Agent"
      },
      "ui": {
        "position": {
          "x": 400,
          "y": 270
        },
        "nodeType": "default"
      },
      "input": [
        {
          "lane": "questions",
          "from": "chat_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "llm_openai_api_1",
      "provider": "llm_openai_api",
      "name": "OpenAI-Compatible API",
      "config": {
        "profile": "custom",
        "tool_choice": "auto",
        "custom": {
          "apikey": "${ROCKETRIDE_GROQ_API_KEY}",
          "base_url": "https://api.groq.com/openai/v1",
          "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b",
          "modelTotalTokens": 2048,
          "modelOutputTokens": 2048,
          "tool_choice": "auto"
        },
        "name": "OpenAI-Compatible API"
      },
      "ui": {
        "position": {
          "x": 700,
          "y": 100
        },
        "nodeType": "default"
      },
